<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
    <%- include('partials/google-tag') %>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Taxi Dispatch System Advice from a Former Operator | Arrington Consultancy</title>
    <%# INDEXABLE TRADE PAGE (Tom, 07/10/2026). No noindex: it is in the
        sitemap and written for the dispatch searches. Not in the main
        navigation. See routes/taxiOperators.js. %>
    <meta name="description" content="Choosing or changing a taxi dispatch system? Independent advice from Tom Arrington, over 20 years in the taxi trade and eight years running on iCabbi. No supplier pays us.">
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/taxi-and-private-hire-operators">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:title" content="Taxi dispatch system advice from a former operator | Arrington Consultancy">
    <meta property="og:description" content="Choosing or changing a taxi dispatch system? Talk to an operator first.">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/taxi-and-private-hire-operators">
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://www.arringtonconsultancy.com/img/logo">
    <meta name="csrf-token" content="<%= csrfToken %>">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400&family=Poppins:wght@500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        :root {
            <% for (const [prop, val] of Object.entries(theme.vars)) { %>
            <%= prop %>: <%= val %>;
            <% } %>
        }
        * { box-sizing: border-box; }
        body { margin: 0; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; background: var(--black); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-styles') %>

        h1, h2, h3 { font-family: 'Poppins', 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-bright); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0; }
        p { color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }

        .btn { display: inline-block; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.6rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid transparent; }
        .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--black); border-color: var(--accent); }
        .btn-primary:hover, .btn-primary:focus-visible { background: var(--accent-hover); border-color: var(--accent-hover); }

        main { padding: 0 0 5rem; }
        .tx-wrap { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }

        /* HERO: the same treatment as the start-up page, with the real photo
           of Tom at his desk (no generated or stock people). A generated rank
           image was considered and left out until a corrected one exists: an
           operator would spot a roof sign on a private hire car at once. */
        .tx-hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: var(--black); display: flex; align-items: center; min-height: 640px; padding: calc(var(--site-chrome) + 3.5rem) 1.5rem 4rem; }
        .tx-hero-photo { position: absolute; top: var(--site-chrome); right: 0; bottom: 0; left: 0; margin: 0; }
        .tx-hero-photo img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 72% 12%; }
        .tx-hero-photo::after { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--black) 0%, var(--black) 28%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--black) 60%, transparent) 52%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--black) 10%, transparent) 78%, transparent 100%), linear-gradient(0deg, var(--black) 0%, transparent 22%); }
        .tx-hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; width: 100%; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }
        .tx-hero-text { max-width: 590px; }

        .tx-label { font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.14em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1rem; display: block; }
        h1 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4.6vw, 2.3rem); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
        .tx-lede { font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--text-bright); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .tx-hero-indep { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }

        .tx-cred { padding: 1.5rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
        .tx-cred p { margin: 0; font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--text-bright); }
        .tx-cred p + p { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.97rem; }

        .tx-section { margin-top: 3.25rem; }
        .tx-section > h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
        .tx-section > p { max-width: 62ch; }

        .tx-dots { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1.4rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .tx-dots li { position: relative; padding-left: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.98rem; color: var(--text); }
        .tx-dots li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
        .tx-dots li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.6em; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); }

        .tx-link { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent); padding-bottom: 2px; }
        .tx-link:hover, .tx-link:focus-visible { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

        /* WAYS TO WORK WITH US: the one band on the paper surface, which is
           reserved for tangible scope. All five core offers at their approved
           prices (Tom, 07/10/2026), each linking to its own page. */
        .tx-band { margin-top: 3.5rem; padding: 3.25rem 0 3.5rem; }
        .tx-band .tx-section { margin-top: 0; }
        .tx-offers { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.4rem 0 0; display: grid; gap: 0.9rem; }
        .tx-offer { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-paper) 70%, white 30%); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; gap: 0.3rem 1.25rem; align-items: baseline; }
        .tx-offer h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; }
        .tx-offer-price { font-family: 'Poppins', 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-bright); text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
        .tx-offer p { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
        .tx-offer .tx-offer-more { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
        .tx-offer-lead { grid-column: 1 / -1; font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); }
        .tx-offers-next { margin: 1.6rem 0 1.1rem; max-width: 62ch; }
        .tx-offers-actions { margin: 0; }

        @media (max-width: 760px) {
            .tx-hero { display: block; min-height: 0; padding: var(--site-chrome) 0 0; }
            .tx-hero-photo { position: relative; top: auto; height: 48vw; max-height: 300px; }
            .tx-hero-photo img { object-position: 66% 25%; }
            .tx-hero-photo::after { background: linear-gradient(0deg, var(--black) 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--black) 40%, transparent) 30%, transparent 60%); }
            .tx-hero-inner { padding: 0 1.5rem 0.5rem; margin-top: -1.5rem; }
            .tx-cred { margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.25rem 0; }
            .tx-section { margin-top: 2.1rem; }
            .tx-band { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding: 2.5rem 0 2.75rem; }
            .tx-offer { padding: 1.15rem 1.2rem; }
            .tx-hero-actions .btn { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
            .tx-lede { font-size: 1.02rem; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('partials/site-header', { currentPage: { slug: 'taxi-and-private-hire-operators' }, navPages, canEdit: false, content, pageContact }) %>

    <%# HERO. The headline names the decision the searcher is facing. Every
        fact below it is evidenced: over 20 years in the trade starting as a
        driver (Tom, 07/10/2026), nearly twenty years owning the business
        (Evidence case study), around eight years on iCabbi and sold in 2025
        (Tom's approved email of 6 July 2026). %>
    <header class="tx-hero">
        <picture class="tx-hero-photo">
            <source srcset="/img/startup/tom-at-desk.webp" type="image/webp">
            <img src="/img/startup/tom-at-desk.jpg" alt="Tom Arrington at his desk" width="1672" height="941" fetchpriority="high">
        </picture>
        <div class="tx-hero-inner">
            <div class="tx-hero-text">
                <span class="tx-label">Taxi and private hire</span>
                <h1>Choosing or changing a taxi dispatch system? Talk to an operator first.</h1>
                <p class="tx-lede">Tom Arrington spent over 20 years in the taxi trade in Devon and Cornwall. He started as a driver, then owned and ran Abacus and Falmouth Taxis for nearly twenty years, around eight of them on iCabbi, before selling the business in 2025.</p>
                <p class="tx-hero-indep" data-independence-hero>We're independent of every dispatch supplier.</p>
                <div class="tx-hero-actions">
                    <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us what's going on</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <main>
        <div class="tx-wrap">
        <%# INDEPENDENCE (Tom, 07/10/2026): no supplier pays us, and the
            iCabbi Marketplace listing is disclosed rather than hidden. %>
        <div class="tx-cred" data-independence>
            <p>We're listed on the iCabbi Marketplace because Tom ran on iCabbi for around eight years. We don't sell software and no supplier pays us.</p>
            <p>We work with operators anywhere in the UK, by video call, and Tom will come and see you in person on request, with travel costs agreed before he sets off.</p>
        </div>

        <%# Built from Tom's approved email of 6 July 2026 (APPROVED 03 in the
            voice folder), recast as "we" with Tom in the third person. %>
        <div class="tx-section">
            <h2>Most of the time it isn't the software</h2>
            <p>When something goes wrong in a taxi office, the dispatch system usually gets the blame. To be fair, sometimes it is the software. More often it's the setup, the pricing, the zones, the drivers, the geography or what everyone expected the system to do, and usually it's a bit of all of them. Changing the system won't fix a problem that sits in the business, and it's an expensive way to find that out.</p>
            <p>Tom has been the operator on the other side of that table. He bought the business at 22, very nearly lost it and rebuilt it, and he's worked with the National Taxi Association. Dealing with drivers, zone profiles, VAT, dispatch, pricing and customers, often all before lunchtime, is something only another operator really appreciates.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tx-section">
            <h2>Choosing or changing a dispatch system</h2>
            <p>Before you sign, we help you work out whether the system is the problem at all, and if it is, what the new one has to do for your operation rather than what looks good in a demo. Tom ran on iCabbi and knows the other main UK systems.</p>
            <p>If you do change, the switchover is where the risk sits:</p>
            <ul class="tx-dots" data-switchover>
                <li>your account customers, and how their bookings and invoices move across</li>
                <li>keeping your phone numbers and making sure calls land in the right place</li>
                <li>getting drivers onto the new app without losing them in the process</li>
                <li>card payments, and how fares and driver settlements work out</li>
                <li>the notice period on the contract you're leaving</li>
                <li>the night you switch over, and who's in the office when you do</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Afterwards, we help you get the most from the system you've chosen, because the setup decides most of what you get out of it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tx-section">
            <h2>The business behind the system</h2>
            <p>Often the question underneath the system is a commercial one: whether your pricing covers the work, whether account customers pay on time, how drivers are paid and kept, and how much of the business still runs through you. That's what our Commercial Review looks at, and it's the same thinking Tom used when he rebuilt his own business. <a class="tx-link" href="/evidence#biography__2">Read the Abacus and Falmouth Taxis story</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tx-section">
            <h2>Websites for operators</h2>
            <p>A taxi website has one job, which is getting the booking. We build HTML sites from scratch, not from a template, around the way your customers book, whether that's a phone call, your app or online, so the number and the app links are where people look for them.</p>
        </div>

        <%# AI is introduced only where it solves a real problem, never as the
            hook (00 Brand OS, AI WORKERS). %>
        <div class="tx-section">
            <h2>The phones and the office</h2>
            <p>A lot of an office's day goes on the same calls: where's my car, what's the fare, can I book for Friday. Where it genuinely helps, we can set up AI to take some of that off the controller's desk, inside rules you set and with a person stepping in whenever it matters.</p>
        </div>
        </div>

        <%# THREE PAID OFFERS with a taxi lead-in each (Tom, 07/10/2026: the
            £3,400 card dropped after the second review). Names, prices and
            descriptions read from lib/whereToStartOffers.js so the page can
            never disagree with the offer pages; the Product Guide covers the
            rest. No credit mechanics here. %>
        <section class="tx-band surface-paper">
        <div class="tx-wrap">
        <div class="tx-section">
            <h2>Ways to work with us</h2>
            <ul class="tx-offers" data-offers="<%= offers.length %>">
                <% offers.forEach(function (o) { %>
                <li class="tx-offer" data-offer-id="<%= o.id %>">
                    <span class="tx-offer-lead"><%= o.taxiLead %></span>
                    <h3><%= o.name %></h3>
                    <span class="tx-offer-price"><%= '£' + (o.pricePence / 100).toLocaleString('en-GB') %></span>
                    <p><%= o.description %></p>
                    <p class="tx-offer-more"><a class="tx-link" href="<%= o.path %>">See the <%= o.name %></a></p>
                </li>
                <% }) %>
            </ul>
            <p class="tx-offers-next">Not sure which fits? Tell us what's going on and Tom will give you a straight view. For everything else we do, see the <a class="tx-link" href="/product-guide">Product Guide</a>.</p>
            <div class="tx-offers-actions">
                <a href="#conversation" class="btn btn-primary">Tell us what's going on</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        </section>

</main>

    <%- include('partials/site-footer', { canEdit: false, pageContact, content }) %>
    <script nonce="<%= nonce %>">
        <%- include('partials/site-chrome-script') %>
    </script>
</body>
</html>
